  "subject": "👟 Axios Finish Line: Little walks",
  "date": "Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:29:31 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🌾 Plus: Dune views | Monday, August 31, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n PRESENTED BY PEPSICO \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Aug 31, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n 🌙 Good evening. Tonight's host is Axios' Ashley May, sharing a simple summer ritual she started with her kids.\n\n Smart Brevity™ count: 309 words … 1 min. Edited by Natalie Daher and copy edited by Amy Stern. \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: 15-minute rituals \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n My favorite 15 minutes of the day are completely ordinary: My kids and I walk around the neighborhood, Axios' Ashley May writes. \n\n Why it matters: This ritual has become the setting for some of my favorite moments and conversations of the year. 💭 My son tells me about his dreams — often literally what he dreamt about last night. My daughter and I try to spot the chirping birds.\n\n Sometimes we don't talk at all. We just move forward together. 📍 There are some ground rules:\n\n No devices allowed. That way, I'm not checking the time or notifications. I bring my coffee with me. I've found that I can sustain only one leisurely morning ritual at a time, so the mug comes along. The dog stays home. He'll get his own walk later, where he'll trot and sniff at whatever pace he wants. 🧭 We don't have a set route. We wander . We've found new gardens, new neighbors and even a garage art gallery.\n\n Exercise scientist and dad Keith Diaz tells me our walks are building a healthy habit that could help my kids buck recent trends.\n\n Research shows children's physical activity drops steadily between ages 6 and 17, with a particularly sharp decline around ages 9 to 12. Daily walks can be \"movement as medicine, but on their level,\" Diaz says. What's next: I know my kids won't always want to walk with me. But maybe one day these walks will help them find their own way.\n\n Share this story . \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM PEPSICO\r\n\n \r\n AI tools built for the farm \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n PepsiCo is using AI to help farmers and agronomists turn field observations into faster, more informed decisions.\n\n\r\n An example: Its AI Agronomy Advisor identifies crop issues, assesses severity and guides practical next steps.\n\n\r\n Read the Q&amp;A. \n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 🌅 Parting shot: Shore thing \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Ashley Corso Summer skies over Long Beach Island, N.J., where reader Ashley Corso captured a pastel evening along the dunes.\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
